-- DICT-SEMANTICS §6.2 "T4 implemented" at a nested `requires` prerequisite, over
-- the prelude's instances.  Each binding's goal selects an instance whose
-- prerequisite is open: `Eq (List ?a)` selects `impl Eq (List a) requires Eq a`,
-- which poses `Eq ?a`.  No literal sits under `?a` (no D3 default), no given and
-- no later binding fixes it, and each interface has two or more instances with no
-- stable minimum.  Hand-derived: REJECT on all three verbs, one
-- T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE per binding, at the expression that poses its goal.
a = [] == []
b = None == None
c = Ok 1 == Ok 1
d = debug []
e = "\{[]}"
f = compare [] []
g = hash None
main = println "unreached"
